<p>Four men affiliated with Mandan have served as North Dakota governor; William Langer started his career here, Frank Briggs moved here, Joseph Devine died here. George Shafer was born in Mandan, the man who became the first native of the state to be elected its chief executive when he was elected governor in 1928. (Note: Walter Maddock, who preceded Shafer, was also born in what would later become the State of North Dakota, but Maddock assumed the role as governor after the death of A.G. Sorlie. He was never elected to the position.)</p>

